# This is the one repository here that is built around pull requests from other people:
# add-on authors submit their own listing under listings/. A listing is metadata only - a
# name, the scopes the add-on asks for, and a link to its own repository - never code.
#
# The catch-all below is what makes GitHub request a review automatically on every such
# pull request, instead of relying on the notification being noticed.
* @lukislp

# The validation contract and everything that runs in CI. A listing pull request has no
# business touching these, so they are called out separately: if one of them shows up in
# the diff of a submission, that is the first thing the review has to explain.
/schema/ @lukislp
/scripts/ @lukislp
/.github/ @lukislp
/LICENSE @lukislp
